==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Dragon Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l King Dragon Cat''' when obtained from [[Tiny Tail (Deadly)|Li'l Lizard Awakens!]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], this unit suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, which, combined with the increased difficulty in getting + levels, makes this unit underperform greatly in his field. For this reason, usage of this unit prior to unlocking their True Form is not recommended unless for his "Attack up" Sm combo with [[Masai Cat]], that can be useful to bring in some stages, especially combined with other Attack up combos.

==='''True Form'''===
Li'l King Dragon Cat becomes exactly the same as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], making him one of the best non-[[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic]] ranged attackers to bring in 4-crown stages. You can also pair Li'l King Dragon with his other variants to create a massive DPS stack, which is one of the main strategies on stages like [[Revenge of Red Sky (Merciless)|Revenge of Red Sky]].

If the player's King Dragon is at a lower level, Li'l King Dragon will actually be the better choice out of the two, and if you have completed [[Li'l Cat's Trial]], they will have similar level caps, ensuring the Li'l variant's superiority with the addition of his Talents.

==='''Talents'''===
While his talents may cost some precious NP, the result is a unit that surpasses his Normal, Brainwashed, and even Manic counterparts.

The first such talent is a mini-wave. While this talent is not guaranteed, nor is it as strong as LKD's base attack, it pierces forward and has an effective area attack. This makes it good for both additional chip and supporting peons. Still, this talent is somewhat expensive, but it does pay its dividends in {{4c}} stages where it can work. Similarly, Attack Up boosts LKD's attacks directly and thus really valuable at enhancing his usage in {{4c}} stages or otherwise.

Survive and HP Up both improve this unit's survivability nicely. HP Up is a more direct way of preserving a stack, while Survive allows LKD to enjoy a final knockback, which works well with his range. Similarly, Surge Immune is a great talent with so many stages relying on Surges for offensive pressure. In fact, since LKD often avoids attacks due to his high range, this immunity is especially important in protecting him against one of the few ways to reach him in the back.

Overall, these talents can be costly together but well worth the investment. This works out especially well, as these talents were introduced in the same update that increases the plus-levels on Li'l Cats.

==='''Orb'''===
Any Attack Up orb works quite well due to how Attack orbs are a flat boost, no matter what multipliers occur. Attack Up against Aku is especially recommended due to his Surge Immunity. Do note that if you got the Surge Immunity Talent, 1-Time Counter-Surge will be useless.

